This repository contains original port orchestration and documentation.
References are not claims of hardware validation or redistribution permission.

Samsung / Linux contributors / ace2nutzer:
  https://github.com/ace2nutzer/Samsung_dreamlte_Kernel
  Candidate Linux kernel source; retain its GPL terms and notices when modifying.
Abdur Rouf:
  https://github.com/roufsweb/galaxy-s8
  G950N native Linux boot reference, not a G955N installation image.
tingao / exynos8895 contributors:
  https://github.com/tingao/dream2lte-droidspaces-kernel
  S8+ container configuration and cgroup patch reference.
Halium / UBports / libhybris / Mesa contributors:
  https://docs.halium.org/
  https://docs.ubports.com/
  https://github.com/libhybris/libhybris
  https://docs.mesa3d.org/drivers/panfrost.html

No Samsung firmware, Mali proprietary libraries, Windows/Ubuntu disk images,
device identifiers or calibration data are distributed by this repository.

Generic Samsung DTBH/Android-v0 packing helpers in scripts/boot/ are reused
from TurboCE/galaxy-s9plus-ubuntu commit
9a15fe0f75669779eb3ee460eccbde229167b248 (GPL-2.0-only), derived from the
SheroAbi/galaxy-s9plus-mainline-linux project and dtbtool-exynos work credited
there. Only source-format helpers are reused; no G965N image, device tree or
firmware is used on G955N. The GPL-2.0 text is included in LICENSE.

Samsung Electronics / LineageOS CP boot contributors:
  https://github.com/LineageOS/android_hardware_samsung_slsi-linaro_exynos
  cpboot_v3 at e9816cf6ed8123a2f20ea334641794a0e64b1e7f (Apache-2.0)
  BootDumpModap and Protocol SIPC RAM-boot sequence references for the native
  bounded implementation in compat/modem/cp_boot.py. Public source pins and
  Apache-2.0 license text are retained there. No vendor firmware/NV is included.

libsamsung-ipc contributors (Joerie de Gram, Simon Busch, Paul Kocialkowski
and other upstream contributors):
  https://github.com/LineageOS/android_external_libsamsung-ipc
  6d244414f7c66b0d0f93ef4b34f5276023408016 (GPL-2.0-or-later)
  Public SIPC wire format, command numbers and NV companion checksum format
  references for the independent native status diagnostic. No original library,
  supported-device claim or vendor RIL is installed by that diagnostic.
